# D27 accept-both, SELF-HOST resolver lane: the canonical `^` move sigil on
# the SELF FACE (`^self`), i.e. a consuming method.
#
# AXIS CELL: glyph = `^` · position = self-face · receiver shape = struct with
# a `&self` sibling method on the same `equip` block (so a partial regression
# that broke only the consuming face would still trip this) · lanes = Rust gg
# (C + LLVM), self-host resolver, self-host runtime.
#
# ⚠ `^self` parses ONLY inside an `equip` block — a bare top-level function
# cannot spell the self face, so this cell necessarily uses `equip`.
#
# The `!self` (retired-glyph) control is the existing corpus; no new `!` site
# is added (the `fmt_no_new_move_bang_in_migrated_corpora` ratchet in
# tests/lints.rs is shrink-only and at zero headroom).
#
# RED-verified against the PRE-port self-host resolver driver by diffing the
# driver's own output on this file: pre-port it emitted `DEF Variable ""` for
# the self-face (the name LOST); post-port it emits `DEF Variable "self"`.
# That one-line delta is this cell's caret pin. Guards the `^self` ownership
# predicate in parser.gg.
#
# ⚠ SCOPE OF THE PIN: this fixture does NOT reach MATCH in
# `resolver_comparison`, for a reason that has nothing to do with D27 — the
# self-host resolver omits a `RES` edge for the `self` receiver inside an
# `equip` method body, so it emits one fewer RES line than Rust gg. That
# divergence is GLYPH-INDEPENDENT: the minimal `&self` probe
# (`int size(&self): return self.text.len()`) diverges identically, and it
# reproduces in a 10-line program with no move sigil anywhere. Filed in
# TODO.md with a repro at
# `tests/fixtures/known_gaps/sh_resolver_equip_self_receiver_res_missing.gg`.
# The shape here is deliberately NOT reworked to dodge it (that would bury
# the gap): the caret pin is the direct pre/post driver-output delta above,
# plus the self-host RUNTIME lane (committed snapshot) and the
# `sh_parser_caret_predicate_siblings` lint in tests/lints.rs.
#
# Expected stdout: 3\nwidget

struct Label:
    String text

equip Label:
    int size(&self):
        return self.text.len()

    String into_text(^self):
        return self.text

void main():
    Label small = Label("abc")
    print(small.size())

    Label owned = Label("widget")
    print(owned.into_text())
